ean for a sequence?","options":["There exists $M$ such that $a_i \\le M$ for all $i \\ge 1$","There exists $M$ such that $a_i = M$ only for $i = 1$","No lower bound is allowed","There exists $M$ such that $a_i \\ge M$ for all $i \\ge 1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4da1aa8816524f4a718ee6a1","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which of the following real sequences, indexed by positive integers $n$, is bounded?","options":["$a_n = n$","$a_n = \\frac{1}{n}$","$a_n = (-1)^n n$","$a_n = 2^n$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"925c93aeeb4d4aab859767b7","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which example is bounded but not convergent?","options":["$a_n = (-1)^n$","$a_n = \\frac{1}{n}$","$a_n = n$","$a_n = 0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1457f329ebb5de4a1aa4b10d","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What is true about convergent sequences?","options":["Every bounded sequence is convergent","Every unbounded sequence is finite","No finite sequence is bounded","Every convergent sequence is bounded"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dece70deb68c5239a54c191b","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $|a_n|\\le 5$ for all $n$, which other inequality also certifies boundedness?","options":["$|a_n|\\le 10$","$|a_n|\\le 2$","$|a_n|\\le 0$","$|a_n|\\le -5$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b26a5a769c3ee3dbc0587830","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $|a_i| \\le 7$ for all $i \\ge 1$, what can be concluded?","options":["$(a_n)$ is unbounded","$(a_n)$ is bounded","$(a_n)$ must converge to $7$","$(a_n)$ is finite"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"777a9d328a9ef9f8d8b6bdd5","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $a_n = (-1)^n$, which $M$ works in $|a_i| \\le M$?","options":["$M = 0$","$M = -1$","$M = \\frac{1}{2}$","$M = 1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ec18b7c31175e9f620ea567c","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $(a_n)$ be a real sequence satisfying $|a_n|\\le M$ for every $n$, where $M\\ge0$. Which statement about $(-a_n)$ is guaranteed?","options":["It is bounded by the same $M$ in absolute value.","It is unbounded unless every term is zero.","It is bounded only if every term is positive.","Its absolute values are $-M$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"71b7293f8f8f031e5a094fea","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement correctly separates boundedness from convergence?","options":["Boundedness implies convergence, but convergence does not imply boundedness","Convergence implies boundedness, but boundedness alone does not imply convergence","The two notions are identical","Neither notion applies to infinite sequences"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"55dd88292d63e8a56d6a091f","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which sequence is bounded from below but not bounded?","options":["$a_n = n$","$a_n = (-1)^n$","$a_n = \\frac{1}{n}$","$a_n = 0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"024130b62fbdc6858897503c","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which conclusion is valid for a finite sequence?","options":["It is always unbounded","It must converge to $0$","It is bounded","It cannot have an upper bound"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2f19a4cc4217db3f9348f039","time_limit":40},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_sequence_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If a real sequence is unbounded, what follows about its convergence?","options":["It must diverge","It must converge","It converges to $0$","Nothing can be concluded"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1612ad6696db5d676547dde5","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_sequence_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does bounded from above mean for $(a_n)$?","options":["There exists $M$ such that $a_i\\le M$ for all $i\\ge1$.","There exists $M$ such that $a_i\\ge M$ for all $i\\ge1$.","There exists $M$ such that $a_i=M$ for exactly one $i$.","There exists $M$ such that $a_i\\ne M$ for all $i$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ab108b62999e9517fc32b5f1","time_limit":35},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_sequence_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What is the smallest $M$ with $|a_n|\\le M$ for $a_n=3+(-1)^n$?","options":["$4$","$2$","$3$","$1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f89afe39d9841e03d57d7b0f","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_sequence_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which $M$ bounds the sequence $a_n=(-1)^n/n$?","options":["$M=0$","$M=1$","$M=-1$","No such $M$ exists."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5de919cc0592b5735418dfa4","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_sequence_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which sequence is unbounded?","options":["$a_n=1/n$","$a_n=(-1)^n$","$a_n=0$","$a_n=n$"],"ans